# Committed artifacts that CI regenerates and diffs byte-for-byte must stay LF
# on every platform: a Windows autocrlf checkout would otherwise render CRLF,
# and the license-ledger --check gate (drift = exit 1) would be red on
# windows-latest while green on ubuntu/macos — not a dependency drift at all.
submission/OSS_LEDGER.md text eol=lf

# Node ESM scripts carry #! shebangs, and vite/vitest fails to transform a
# shebang'd .mjs whose line endings are CRLF (reproduced 2026-09-02: hosted
# windows-latest checkout rendered scripts/verify-exploration-sandbox.mjs with
# CRLF and both suite imports died with "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected
# token"; the identical LF tree was green locally and on ubuntu). LF-only .mjs
# removes the platform-dependent parse failure class entirely.
*.mjs text eol=lf
